WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.350
A new trailer is out for Westworld Season
2, and it reveals lots about the character

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.490
arcs and themes of the new season, as well
as some glimpses at the deepest secrets of

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.110
Westworld.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:16.810
Bernard wakes up on a beach with the sort
of hangover you can only get from finding

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:21.930
out that you’re a robot and your whole life
is a lie and also the sea’s full of corpses.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.199
Bernard has some thinking to do.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:25.560
Who is he now?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.069
What does his life mean?

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:31.369
And after Dolores’ robot uprising, whose
side is he on?

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:33.150
Is he with his robot brethren?

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.750
Or with the humans he’s lived with all his
life?

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:42.280
We see Bernard with human security forces
including Charlotte, Stubbs, and new characters

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.750
Maling and Karl.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.590
But Charlotte discovers a bunch of old Bernard
hosts.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:52.630
How will she and the other humans react when
they find out that Bernard is a machine?

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:55.360
How can they trust him?

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.110
Dolores is enjoying her new freedom.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:02.130
But she’s also waging a brutal war against
humans.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:07.120
She captures and hangs people, she says it’s
a “reckoning”, justice for the terrible

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.760
things humans did to hosts . But it’s also
a fight for survival.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.610
“It's us or them” she says.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:19.830
With Dolores is her army of masked men, and
Clementine, and Teddy.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:24.510
Teddy seems to be the angel on Dolores’
shoulder, politely suggesting that violent

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.130
genocide might not be the right thing to do.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:33.479
“Is this really what you want?” he asks
. Dolores meets Maeve, and she also questions

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:38.970
Dolores – Maeve suggests that taking violent
revenge makes you just as bad as the humans

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.690
are .
Maeve’s goal is to reunite with her robot

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:43.690
daughter.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:48.420
So she confronts Sizemore and demands that
he help her . Sizemore points out that Maeve’s

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:54.460
daughter is just a robot, a machine programmed
to play a role – it’s not really her daughter

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.549
. But Maeve wants her anyway.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:03.120
Maybe the idea here is that the only meaning
in life is what we choose to value, so there’s

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.830
beauty in Maeve’s love for her daughter
even if it’s artificial.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:12.030
We see Maeve in Shogun World, the Japanese-themed
Delos park.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:18.280
Which is weird, because last season, Felix
said that Maeve’s daughter is in Park 1.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:23.800
And on the Delos website, it looks like Westworld
is Park 1, not Shogun World – so why is

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.520
Maeve there?

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.990
Maybe the entrance to Westworld is locked
down, so Maeve has to take a detour through

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.270
Shogun World to get in.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:36.090
Maybe she’ll also see some of the other
four parks.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.950
Westworld security forces mop up what’s
left after Dolores’ massacre.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:45.750
And later it looks like they get in a fight
with the Confederados, the ex-confederate

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.950
soldier hosts from last season.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.950
Charlotte, meanwhile, has her own mission.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:56.100
A video hidden on the Delos website shows
Charlotte’s name along with the words “Find

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.330
Peter Abernathy”.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:03.560
Peter is the host who Charlotte tried to use
to smuggle data out of Westworld last season.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.640
Her plan failed when Peter disappeared from
host cold storage.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.410
It looks like now, Charlotte’s trying to
get him back.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:18.000
So all of this stuff is happening in the present
of Westworld, but Season 2, like last season,

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.290
uses a non-linear timeline.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:24.129
Some parts of the story are set decades in
the past.

00:03:24.129 --> 00:03:29.849
So we see Dolores with Arnold, the original
human Bernard from thirty years ago.

00:03:29.849 --> 00:03:34.640
And he tells her that dreams “don't mean
anything” – but Dolores doesn’t like

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:40.269
that answer . Maybe because, according to
Ford, “dreams mean everything” – they

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:46.410
represent the people “who we could become”
. So maybe Dolores is now angry that she was

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.989
held back from her destiny for so long.

00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:54.830
We see Dolores after sex with Logan – it
looks like they’re both at this party or

00:03:54.830 --> 00:04:01.040
corporate gig in some real world-looking city
– so this could be New York – or maybe

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.959
it’s another park, Futureworld or something.

00:04:03.959 --> 00:04:06.959
We also see Logan naked in the desert.

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:12.140
Maybe this is what happened to Logan after
William tied him naked to a horse last season.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:16.600
It looks like we’ll learn more about William
and Logan’s conflict, and how William took

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.760
over the Westworld corporation, Delos.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:25.639
In the trailer, we see James Delos, the founder
of the company, walking angrily from Logan

00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:28.510
– who is possibly James’ son.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:33.980
James seems a complicated character, we see
him bloodied at a broken mirror in a hidden

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:36.270
video on the Westworld site.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.220
And we see young William meeting Dolores.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:44.490
But this isn’t the conscious humanlike Dolores
he fell in love with last season – this

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.880
Dolores looks wiped, and unconscious.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:54.070
Maybe the pain of seeing the woman he loved
reduced to a machine is part of what led William

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:59.470
to become the Man in Black .
Last season, the Man in Black wanted the violence

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:04.210
in Westworld to become real and dangerous
and challenging – and now, he’s got his

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:09.750
wish . So why does he put a gun to his head,
and talk about burning it to the ground ? In

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:14.120
Season 1, Ford tells the story of a greyhound
that chases a cat.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.750
When it catches and kills the cat, it gets
confused, and doesn’t know what to do next

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.220
. Maybe old William is the same.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:25.590
He got what he wanted, so now he needs a new
purpose.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:30.110
He might find purpose in a quest for the door.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:35.170
Season 2 of Westworld is titled The Door,
and we see William approaching the entrance

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.290
of some bunker.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:43.110
He’s also seen here with the broken body
of Robert, the robot version of young Ford.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:47.240
And Robert appears in hidden video saying
“now you’re in my game.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.040
And this game is find the door”.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:55.020
Maybe this will be another cryptic quest to
keep William busy for another season.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:59.590
Or maybe it’s a chance for him to break
out of his empty cycle of violence, and to

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:02.610
find new meaning in life.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:07.010
Finally, we see more of these mysterious drone
hosts.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:11.830
Showrunner Jonathan Nolan says they’re connected
to the Delos corporation’s “secret project”

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:16.970
in Westworld . Maybe this red technology stuff
is also involved – it sure looks like some

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:22.629
super important vibranium unobtanium special
nano stuff so… keep an eye on that.

00:06:22.629 --> 00:06:26.910
[] But it’s anyone’s guess what exactly
Delos’s project is.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:32.610
In the 1976 Westworld sequel Futureworld,
Delos makes robot clones to replace world

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:36.240
leaders and take over the world – so it
could be something like that.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.060
Or maybe it’s a military technology thing.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.210
Or human consciousness research.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:46.039
In Season 1, Charlotte suggests it’s related
to the data hidden in Peter’s head, so maybe

00:06:46.039 --> 00:06:50.060
her quest is key to Delos’ big secret.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.220
So there’s a lot going on here.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:57.660
Westworld continues to tell a complex non-linear
story, exploring identity, consciousness,

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:01.540
meaning on a backdrop splattered with violence
and sex.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:06.270
This promises to be another intense season
of TV.

